yaca: General-purpose terminal agent.

Usage:
  yaca [directory]
  yaca --help [topic]
  yaca --version
  yaca --self-test [options]
  yaca --model-repl
  yaca --config-repl
  yaca --context-repl recent|full
  yaca --continue <selector>
  yaca --export [selector]
  yaca --status

Canonical actions:
  --help             -h     /h     Show registry-generated help without loading configuration.
  --version          -v     /v     Show product, version, and release-target identity.
  --self-test        -st    /st    Run ordered diagnostics through Stage 1, 2, or 3.
  --model-repl       -mr    /mr    Open the offline-safe Model management REPL.
  --config-repl      -cfg   /cfg   Open the offline-safe configuration REPL.
  --context-repl     -ctx   /ctx   Open the Context browser in recent or full view.
  --continue         -c     /c     Continue one Context selected by short name or precise hash.
  --export           -ex    /ex    Export a selected or current Context through the public format.
  --status           -stt   /stt   Show status for the explicitly opened current Context.

Embedded Lua (handled before application startup):
  yaca --lua [Lua options] [script [args]]
  yaca --lua -v                 Show the linked Lua version.
  yaca --lua -E -e <code>       Run code without Lua environment initialization.
  yaca --lua -E -               Read a script from standard input.
  No configuration or Model is needed; ordinary exec permissions still apply.

Self-test options:
  --through-stage 1|2|3
  --list-checks
  --exclude-model <value> (repeatable)
  --exclude-check <value> (repeatable)
  --check <value> (repeatable)
  --i-accept-online-self-test

Global modifier:
  --machine  Emit versioned JSON/JSONL for help, version, or offline Stage 1.

Rules:
  -- ends option parsing; use it before a directory beginning with '-'.
  / aliases are recognized only on Windows; Linux / paths stay positional.
  Interactive actions require both stdin and stdout to be terminals.
  Short Context name selects the first usable match; use hash for precision.

Topics: chat, context, input, actions, or any semantic action ID.
